# The native bindings toolchain is line-ending sensitive: tools/valdi-rolldown/codegen.ts
# writes LF, and its --check byte-compares the result with the checked-in bindings that the
# export scripts verify on every platform. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites the sources and generated files to CRLF, which changes the generated C++ headers
# and fails the check. Check out LF everywhere except batch files, which keep CRLF for cmd.exe.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
